From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: parts for EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN (a bounded GPU wait, the allocator's use, a read-only walk of the deleted buffers); nothing calls them without the switch

What: four small parts 0801 and 0802 use, with no caller of their own.
- MasterSemaphore::WaitFor(tick, timeout_ns): MasterSemaphore::Wait with a time limit, true when
  the GPU reached the tick. Timeline path: one vkWaitSemaphores with the timeout, then Refresh.
  Fence path: looks at the tick every 200 us until the deadline. No stall report (the hang watch's
  on_stall stays with Wait).
- MemoryAllocator::UsedBytes(): VMA's allocationBytes over all heaps (vmaGetHeapBudgets, as the
  port's eden_vma_usage reads it), to say what a drain freed.
- DelayedDestructionRing::ForEach(f): calls f for each object still in the ring, reads only.
- BufferCache::DeletedWaiting() (count and bytes of the deleted buffers in the ring, a walk) and
  BufferCache::RetryRefusedNow() (buffer_refused_size back to ~0, so the next request of any size
  asks the allocator again instead of waiting out the 250 ms refusal window).

Off: nothing changes; the new functions are not called.
Merge note: T153's 0698 (EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_MIB) keeps a byte ring next to the same
delayed_destruction_ring; DeletedWaiting walks the ring instead, so the two do not touch each
other's code. ReleaseFinished (which 0698 extends with pending_destroy.Clear()) is what 0801 calls.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 9aa1383e67..96b1a9710a 100644
